# xbindkeys config for the i3 rice -- NOT ~/.xbindkeysrc (xbindkeys reads
# that path by default; this one is launched explicitly with -f from
# i3/config's autostart so it doesn't collide with any other xbindkeys use
# on this machine). Its only job here is the desktop right-click menu
# ("桌面右鍵選單"): a global passive grab on button 3 that replays the
# click normally (xbindkeys does this by default -- it never consumes/
# blocks the event) and ALSO runs desktop-menu.sh, which checks whether
# the click actually landed on bare desktop background before showing
# anything. See desktop-menu.sh's own comment for why that check is safe.
"~/.config/i3/desktop-menu.sh"
    b:3
